=== REASONING ===
Implementation maps 1:1 to the contract clauses R1-R7 and tests W1-W7
specified by Prompt 05:

  R1 (value preserved bit-for-bit): RestampLegacy decodes via
    decodeLegacySignalValue then re-encodes via
    encodeTimestampedSignalValue. The encoder marshals the typed value
    through json.Marshal so float64 stays float64, bool stays bool,
    strings stay strings, JSON objects stay objects.

  R2 (only legacy entries restamped): RestampLegacy attempts envelope
    parse and skips when ok=true && err=nil. Fresh envelopes are
    NEVER added to the restamp HSet payload, so their Timestamp is
    preserved bit-for-bit (verified by W2 byte snapshot).

  R3 (idempotent / safe to retry): A second Warm call observes that
    every field is now a valid envelope, builds an empty restamp
    payload, returns early before HSet/Expire are issued. W3 asserts
    C2 == C1 == 1 (no additional HSet writes on the second call).

  R4 (partial-failure safe): Warm calls RestampLegacy first; if HSet
    fails, RestampLegacy returns the wrapped error WITHOUT having
    issued any HDEL/DEL. Warm wraps via the existing 'warm live
    signals from Redis for vehicle %d: %w' format and returns BEFORE
    calling hydrateMissingValues, so L1 is not mutated. W4 verifies
    all three fields are intact, fresh envelope bytes preserved,
    legacy entries unchanged, L1 nil.

  R5 (L1 hydrated after restamp): Warm re-reads via GetAllValues
    after RestampLegacy succeeds. Restamped entries now carry
    non-zero Timestamps and flow through hydrateMissingValues (the
    Timestamp.IsZero() skip was removed). The skip-when-exists
    branch preserves live-wins for pre-existing L1 entries. W5
    verifies legacy Odometer hydrates into L1 while pre-existing
    L1 BatteryLevel (80) wins over restamped Redis BatteryLevel (72).

  R6 (TTL refreshed): RestampLegacy issues Expire(ctx, key,
    signalKeyTTL) after the HSet (same call shape as Update). W6
    instruments fakeRedisSignalClient.expireCalls and asserts at
    least one call for the right key/duration.

  R7 (no key/channel rename, no field deletion): RestampLegacy uses
    the existing key fmt.Sprintf("vehicle:%d:signals", ...) and
    issues only HSet (variadic) + Expire — no HDEL, no DEL. The
    redisSignalClient interface itself does not declare HDel/Del,
    so the production code is structurally incapable of issuing
    them. W4 asserts post-failure hash still contains all original
    fields.

  W7 (existing test transition): The obsolete
    TestHybridLiveSignalStoreWarmSkipsTimestamplessRedisForHistoryHydrate
    test was DELETED. Prompt 05 explicitly allowed deletion in
    favour of W1, which now covers the legacy-restamp + hydrate path.

